CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* array of one: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* const array: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
N5008 [expr.ref]/2: the first operand of `->' is converted to a pointer; an
array undergoes the array-to-pointer conversion ([conv.array]), as with
gmp's `mpz_t x; x->_mp_d'.  Only class operands use an overloaded operator->.
